# Testing & completion

A task is **not complete** because TypeScript compiles or the agent claims it works.

## Verify by impact (run what applies)

| Touch area | Minimum checks |
| --- | --- |
| Any frontend change | Relevant Vitest; lint affected frontend code. If the repository-wide lint cannot reasonably run because of unrelated pre-existing failures, run the narrowest applicable lint/check and explicitly report the remaining limitation; browser console + failed network requests |
| CSS / shared styles / shell | `npm run check:css` (cwd `frontend`) |
| Modals / overlays | `npm run check:modals` (also part of `npm run build`) |
| Build-sensitive / release | `npm run build` in `frontend` |
| QMS | `npm run test:quality` (+ planner/overview scripts if touched); relevant Playwright |
| Tenant shell / nav | `npm run test:tenant-shell` |
| Platform / realtime client | `npm run test:platform` |
| Rostering chunks | `npm run perf:rostering` (and browser measure if load path changed) |
| User journey | Relevant Playwright under `frontend/tests/e2e` when workflow risk is high |
| Backend API/schema | Existing backend tests for that app; do not ship contract drift |

## Workflow bar

- Confirm the actual user path in the browser when UI changed (not only unit tests).
- Every exposed control: working or clearly unavailable.
- Report exact commands run and outcomes. If a check cannot run, say why and what remains unverified.
- Do not treat an unexplained 4xx/5xx browser request as acceptable merely because the visible UI renders.

## Independent verification

For non-trivial work, use the `verifier` subagent against the **original requirement** — do not treat the implementer’s “done” as evidence.
